@startuml adxl-status-repeat
' When the accelerometer status speaks, and when the sensor is configured.
' Grounded in Src/adxl_report.c (adxl_report_update) and Src/main.c, where
' the call sits after the update-session check on purpose.

title The repeated status, once every two seconds

skinparam shadowing false

start

:called from the loop with now_ms;

if (ADXL_REPORT_PERIOD_MS passed\nsince the last line?) then (no)
  :return 0, nothing sent;
  note right
    The loop runs at megahertz.
    Compared by SUBTRACTION, so a
    clock that wraps after 49 days
    does not go quiet.
  end note
  stop
else (yes)
endif

if (already brought up?) then (yes)
  note right
    The probe writes configuration
    registers. Writing them again
    would restart the sensor's FIFO
    under whoever is reading it.
  end note
else (no)
  :presence = probe()\n(adxl345_begin over I2C1);
  if (READY?) then (yes)
    :brought_up = 1;
  else (no)
    note right
      Tried again next period, so
      wiring the sensor correctly on
      a RUNNING board recovers with
      no reset and no reflash.
    end note
  endif
endif

:send one line through the sink;
note right
  adxl,ready | adxl,wrong | adxl,absent
  Never a number: a sentinel value is
  one the host cannot tell apart from
  a reading.
end note

:return 1;

stop

legend bottom
  It replaced a line sent once at start-up. On 2026-11-02 the monitor
  opened a few milliseconds late and caught "adx" instead of the line,
  and a later reset produced nothing at all. A status that is true for
  one millisecond cannot be read by a person, and a demo is read by a
  person.
endlegend

@enduml
